  "editable": false,
  "description": "Part IV §68 gate 7: 'dashboards/alerts exist for sockets, queue age, routing orphan count, DLQ, DB/query health, channel errors and security anomalies.'\n\nSix of the seven are here. CHANNEL ERRORS is deliberately absent: starlink_channel_send_failures_total has no producer because no external channel adapter is wired — D-01 chose web chat, and the WhatsApp/SMS/email adapters are unbuilt. A panel over a series nothing can emit would be the same silence this dashboard exists to remove. It lands with the first channel adapter.\n\nEvery panel below references a metric that something actually emits; infrastructure/guards/src/alerts-have-producers.test.ts fails the build otherwise.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Sockets (§68 gate 7 · §32.4 reconnect storm)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "description": "A realtime node's live connections and the rate at which they are established. Both series existed as definitions and were emitted by nothing until 2026-08-29; the gateway had no /metrics endpoint at all.",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Live connections per node",
      "description": "Labelled by node because §33's target topology is several gateway nodes behind a load balancer. A node at zero while others carry traffic is the case RealtimeNodeWithNoConnections watches for.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "starlink-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "starlink-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "starlink_active_connections",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A"
